.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KDF 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kdf
.Nd space used by every dataset in the root pool, with compression and quotas
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is
.Xr df 1
for a ZFS system: one line per dataset in
.Li rpool ,
sorted by name, with
.Bl -tag -width "MOUNTPOINT" -compact
.It Li USED
the space it and its descendants take;
.It Li AVAIL
the space it can still grow into, which a quota lowers;
.It Li RATIO
how far compression shrank what it holds;
.It Li QUOTA
its quota, or
.Ql - ;
.It Li MOUNTPOINT
where it is mounted, or
.Ql none
and
.Ql -
for one that is not.
.El
.Pp
Then the pool: its size, what is allocated, what is free, and how
fragmented its free space is.
.Pp
On a terminal, ratios above 1.0 and above 1.5 are coloured; piped, the
output is plain text.
Dataset names are shown without the leading
.Ql rpool/ .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Printed.
.It 1
There is no pool named
.Li rpool .
.It 2
An argument was given.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kdf

