# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql kldload/secrets
has a quota of 100M, so it can grow by 99.8M whatever the pool has free.
.Pp
Only the rows of one part of the tree:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kdf | grep ' home'
  home                                  933G    186G  1.05x       -  /home
  home/anthony                          933G    186G  1.05x       -  /home/anthony
  home/anthony/games                   31.8G    186G  1.39x       -  /home/anthony/games
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr df 1 ,
.Xr kdir 8 ,
.Xr ksnap 8 ,
.Xr zfs-list 8 ,
.Xr zpool-list 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Fl -help
printed the table, since nothing read the arguments; the colours'
escape codes went into pipes; the pool's own row was listed by a filter
that never matched; and the rule under the header was a column short,
drawn in characters three bytes wide and padded by bytes.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Only
.Li rpool
is shown; other pools need
.Ql zfs list .
.Pp
.Li USED
counts snapshots and descendants, so a dataset's row is not what
.Xr du 1
finds under its mountpoint.
